# 1. CRITICAL DEVELOPMENT INSTRUCTION

Build a complete, functional, production-quality web application called Festivo AI.

DO NOT build:

* A static website.
* A frontend-only prototype.
* A landing page with nonfunctional buttons.
* A collection of disconnected UI screens.
* A fake dashboard containing hardcoded statistics.
* A mock AI chatbot.
* A design-only demonstration.
* An MCP-based application.
* A database-dependent application.

Build a complete working full-stack Next.js application.

Every major button, navigation item, form, dialog, and feature must work.

The application must support actual event creation, AI generation, editing, budgeting, task management, vendor management, guest management, and local data persistence.

Use Google Gemini API for AI functionality.

The application must work with only ONE external API credential:

GEMINI_API_KEY

Do not require:

* OpenAI API keys.
* Anthropic API keys.
* Supabase credentials.
* Firebase credentials.
* Database credentials.
* Cloudinary credentials.
* Third-party AI services.
* MCP servers.
* External business APIs.
* External authentication services.

The application must remain useful even when the Gemini API key is not configured. Non-AI features must continue working.

If the existing project contains broken CSS, broken dependencies, or incomplete implementations, inspect and repair them before adding features.

Do not simply create new components while leaving existing errors unresolved.

