# 8. GEMINI API IMPLEMENTATION

## 8.1 API Key

Use:

GEMINI_API_KEY=your_actual_key

Store it in:

.env.local

Create:

.env.example

Never commit the real key.

Never expose the key through NEXT_PUBLIC variables.

## 8.2 Server-Side Integration

Create:

lib/ai/gemini.ts

This file should initialize the official Google GenAI SDK.

Create server endpoints:

POST /api/ai/generate-plan

POST /api/ai/chat

POST /api/ai/generate-moodboard

All endpoints must validate incoming data.

All Gemini requests must happen on the server.

## 8.3 Model Configuration

Use a currently supported Gemini model available to the configured API key.

Keep the model name in one centralized configuration variable.

Do not scatter model identifiers throughout the project.

Do not hardcode an outdated model name.

## 8.4 Structured Responses

Use Gemini structured output where supported.

Validate responses using Zod.

The application must reject invalid output.

Generate IDs in application code.

Convert dates into valid application date formats.

Do not trust AI-generated financial calculations.

## 8.5 Error Handling

Handle:

* Invalid API key.
* Quota exhaustion.
* Rate limiting.
* Network errors.
* Timeout.
* Invalid output.
* Empty response.

Display useful error messages.

Provide retry functionality.

Preserve user inputs and saved data.

If Gemini is unavailable, the rest of the website must continue working.

